18. Important correction to your current Key Vault configuration

You currently have:

data "azurerm_key_vault_secret" "mysecret" {
  name         = "winpass"
  key_vault_id = data.azurerm_key_vault.mywinvault.id
}

That is fine if this project needs the secret, but don't put the secret value into GitHub.

Also don't commit:

terraform.tfstate
terraform.tfstate.backup
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars

Create .gitignore:

.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
crash.log
crash.*.log


*.pem
*.key

If you have a public GitHub repository, never commit passwords, service-principal secrets, SSH private keys, or Key Vault secret values.

Your .pub SSH key is generally okay to distribute, but the corresponding private key must stay private.

