Your project has now become a reusable Terraform platform:

                         GitHub
                           │
             terraform-azure-web-platform
                           │
             ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
             │             │             │
             ▼             ▼             ▼
        Networking       Compute     Load Balancer
          Module          Module          Module
             │             │             │
             ▼             ▼             ▼
           VNet           NICs            LB
             │             │               │
           Subnet          │          Backend Pool
             │             │               │
            NSG            │          Health Probe
             │             │               │
             └─────────────┼───────────────┘
                           │
                           ▼
                        Azure
                           │
                    ┌──────┴──────┐
                    ▼             ▼
                  VM001         VM002
                  NGINX         NGINX
                    └──────┬──────┘
                           │
                           ▼
                    Load Balancer
                           │
                           ▼
                     Public IP

And your Terraform state is separate:

Terraform
    │
    ▼
Azure Storage Account
    │
    └── tfstate
          │
          └── sky-project.tfstate

The key learning point is that modules contain reusable infrastructure logic, variables provide inputs, outputs expose information between modules, and the root module orchestrates everything. Your local machine only needs the root configuration, while terraform init downloads the reusable modules from
